{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["And the reason of <b>He is your praise and He is your Elohim</b>: He shall be your praise, that you shall direct all your praise to Him — Him shall you praise always, and you shall not give His honor to another, nor His praise to idols, nor to the elohim and lords mentioned. Or it may say \"He is your praise\" in the sense that through Him you are praised among all the nations, in the language of <i>For You are the glory of their strength</i> (Psalms 89:18), <i>YHWH is my strength and my stronghold</i> (Jeremiah 16:19)." "<b>And He is your Elohim</b> — for He singled out His name upon you, that you shall be to Him for a people and He shall be to you for Elohim, and not like the rest of the nations, for whom He is <i>Elohei ha-Elohim</i> (Elohim of the elohim) whom He apportioned to them, as I have explained (Leviticus 18:25), for He has done with you the great and awesome things, through which you will recognize that you are His portion and His inheritance and His eyes are always upon you for good."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The closing citation from Jeremiah 16:19 reads 'YHWH my strength and my refuge'; the translator renders ומעוזי literally as 'and my stronghold,' noting that the received verse text has מחסי ('my refuge'). Ramban may be citing a variant or paraphrasing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:45.063765426Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}